    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2002-p58.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "6. Certainly \\(a_{13} \\geq 2\\), so \\(a_{14}\\) is divisible by \\(2^{2}=4\\). Writing \\(a_{14}=4 k\\), we have \\(a_{15}=2^{4 k}=16^{k}\\). But every power of 16 ends in 6 , so this is the answer.",
